,31716,497,379,317,1502,31732,33,8,57960,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,22,24984,220,19,1124,408,90,5187,2555,31716,497,856,488,379,317,1502,31732,34,8,57960,7265,90,5187,2555,92,481,19,14,22,24984,220,16,1124,408,90,5187,2555,31716,497,220,17,18481,488,379,317,1502,31732,35,8,57960,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,24984,220,22,14,19,1124,408,90,5187,2555,31716,497,220,18,18481,488,379,317,1502,31732,36,8,57960,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,19,24984,481,23,1124,408,90,5187,2555,31716,497,320,15,11,15,1106,1502,31732,37,8,57960,7265,90,5187,2555,92,481,16,17,24984,220,17,16,1124,408,90,5187,2555,31716,497,856,317,1502,31732,38,8,57960,7265,90,5187,2555,92,481,17,24984,481,22,14,17,1124,408,90,5187,2555,31716,497,220,17,18481,317,1502,31732,39,8,57960,7265,90,5187,2555,92,481,16,14,18,24984,220,22,14,16,17,1124,408,90,5187,2555,31716,497,220,18,18481,317,24157,6405,2533,6269,279,11931,315,279,4396,2606,11,18663,553,76602,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nA line has slope $-\\frac{7}{4}.$  Which of the following vectors are possible direction vectors for the line?\n\n[asy]\nusepackage(\"amsmath\");\n\nunitsize(1 cm);\n\npair x = (3,0), y = (0,2);\n\nlabel(\"(A) $\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$\", y);\nlabel(\"(B) $\\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$\", x + y);\nlabel(\"(C) $\\begin{pmatrix} -4/7 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$\", 2*x + y);\nlabel(\"(D) $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 7/4 \\end{pmatrix}$\", 3*x + y);\nlabel(\"(E) $\\begin{pmatrix} 14 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}$\", (0,0));\nlabel(\"(F) $\\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}$\", x);\nlabel(\"(G) $\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -7/2 \\end{pmatrix}$\", 2*x);\nlabel(\"(H) $\\begin{pmatrix} -1/3 \\\\ 7/12 \\end{pmatrix}$\", 3*x);\n[/asy]\n\nEnter the letters of the correct options, separated by commas.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"20f5d0c1a204343230e3823f9ac963fcde14d1fdffca5dbb0fd56e2fb2aaca09"},"seconds":46.99617052078247,"seed":30630792671666976,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to determine which of the given vectors could serve as direction vectors for a line with a slope of $-\\frac{7}{4}$. A direction vector for a line with slope $m$ can be represented as $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ m \\end{pmatrix}$ or any scalar multiple of this vector. Since the slope $m = -\\frac{7}{4}$, we need to check which of the given vectors are scalar multiples of $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{4} \\end{pmatrix}$.\n\n### Checking Each Option:\n- **Option (A): $\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$**\n  - This vector has components that do not match the slope $-\\frac{7}{4}$, since $\\frac{7}{4}$ does not equal $-\\frac{7}{4}$.\n\n- **Option (B): $\\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$**\n  - This vector also has components that do not match the required slope since $\\frac{4}{7}$ does not equal $-\\frac{7}{4}$.\n\n- **Option (C): $\\begin{pmatrix} -\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$**\n  - The slope represented by this vector is $-\\frac{7}{4}$ when simplified, as $\\frac{1}{-\\frac{4}{7}} = -\\frac{7}{4}$.\n\n- **Option (D): $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{4} \\end{pmatrix}$**\n  - The slope here is $\\frac{7}{4}$, which is the positive counterpart of $-\\frac{7}{4}$, so this does not match.\n\n- **Option (E): $\\begin{pmatrix} 14 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}$**\n  - This can be scaled to $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{7} \\end{pmatrix}$, which simplifies to the slope $-\\frac{7}{4}$.\n\n- **Option (F): $\\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}$**\n  - This vector can be scaled to $\\begin{pmatrix} -\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$, which matches the slope $-\\frac{7}{4}$.\n\n- **Option (G): $\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} \\end{pmatrix}$**\n  - The slope of this vector is $\\frac{-\\frac{7}{2}}{-2} = \\frac{7}{4}$, which does not match the required slope of $-\\frac{7}{4}$.\n\n- **Option (H): $\\begin{pmatrix} -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{7}{12} \\end{pmatrix}$**\n  - The slope of this vector is $\\frac{\\frac{7}{12}}{-\\frac{1}{3}} = -\\frac{7}{4}$, which matches the required slope.\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe vectors that match the required slope of $-\\frac{7}{4}$ are options (C), (E), (F), and (H).\n\nTherefore, the answer is \\boxed{C,E,F,H}."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{C,E,F,H}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
